---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  route="quiz"
  canonicalPath="/en/privacy/"
  alternatePath="/pt-br/privacidade/"
  indexable={false}
  showGameNavigation={false}
  pageMeta={{
    title: "Privacy and analytics",
    description: "How K-pop Quiz uses visit analytics, cookies and consent choices.",
  }}
>
  <div data-testid="game-shell">
  <article id="privacy-notice" class="privacy-notice" data-testid="privacy-content">
    <p class="kicker">K-pop Quiz</p>
    <h1>Privacy and analytics</h1>
    <p>Updated November 14, 2026.</p>

    <h2>Controller and contact</h2>
    <p>K-pop Quiz determines how this site configures analytics. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:email@pedrosatin.com">email@pedrosatin.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>Browsing data</h2>
    <p>Cloudflare processes technical request data to deliver the site and reduce abuse. This data may include IP address, traffic routing, system configuration, and traffic information. Cloudflare handles this data under its <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/policies/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <p>Cloudflare Web Analytics measures visited pages and performance. Cloudflare states that the tool does not use its own cookies or collect personal data. This measurement remains active regardless of the choice about Google Analytics.</p>

    <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
    <p>Google Analytics 4 loads only after you agree. It uses cookies and identifiers to measure use of the site and produce audience statistics. Google processes this data under its <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <p>With your consent, the site records events at the start, the end and the sharing of a round. These events report the game, the language and, in the quiz, the mode. Start and end events also report whether the round was the daily challenge or free play. The end event reports how the round finished, as a win, a loss or a give-up, and two bands calculated on your device from your local statistics: how many days ago you last played that game and the length of your streak in it. The site does not send your answers, artist names, shared text or its own player or challenge identifiers.</p>

    <h2>Analytics choices</h2>
    <p>The banner lets you accept or reject Google Analytics cookies and identifiers. Cloudflare Web Analytics continues measuring site usage. The banner disappears after your choice. Use the "Privacy preferences" button in the footer to change your choice. Rejecting Google Analytics stops new GA4 measurement on this and later visits.</p>

    <h2>Game feedback</h2>
    <p>After you finish a quiz, the site may ask whether you enjoyed it. Answering is optional. If you vote, your browser sends the vote and the site language to TBBC, the rating service at <code>tbbc.app</code>, with the site’s public key and the fixed labels <code>quiz-result</code> and <code>ponder-club</code>. If you then write a comment, it goes to the same service. The requests carry no cookies, no referrer and no player or game identifier. As with any direct connection, TBBC receives network data such as your IP address. TBBC stores the vote and the comment. Please don’t include personal information in the comment.</p>

    <h2>Sharing and retention</h2>
    <p>Cloudflare metrics are available in the Cloudflare dashboard. Accepted GA4 metrics are available in the site’s Google Analytics property for the retention period configured there. Feedback votes and comments stay with TBBC. The site does not sell browsing data.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask about data processing, correct data, request deletion where applicable, or revoke GA4 consent. Use the email above.</p>
  </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
